author John Crispin <john@phrozen.org> 1792080000 +0200
committer John Crispin <john@phrozen.org> 1792086215 +0200

interface: accept only plain words in the tc arguments

cmd_add_qdisc() appends bandwidth_up, bandwidth_down, mode and the
options to a tc command line that qosify_run_cmd() runs through sh -c.
check_str() refused only a single quote, so a value with a shell
separator ran a command as root. It now refuses every byte outside
letters, digits, '.', '_', '-' and the space that separates option
words. A refused mode keeps the default diffserv4, so the command
never carries "(null)".

Signed-off-by: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
